Attachment bytes are never reclaimed. Design §16 of docs/media-attachments/design.html (reference-counted byte GC) owns all byte reclamation and is not built:

- claw-back on revoke or leave;
- unreferencing replaced or deleted media;
- quota eviction;
- `staged` records that were never promoted.

`byteStore.purgeWorkspace` (src/plugins/attachments/byteStore.ts) is the primitive meant for it, and it has no live caller (checked 2026-10-22). Until the GC lands, local and remote attachment storage only grows. That is the design's intended err-toward-retention posture, accepted at current fleet size.

Why it is hard: the reference count is client-side only, because the content hash sits in encrypted properties. So the sweep must:
- count live, soft-deleted and `blocks_history` references;
- run only on settled, synced state;
- apply a grace window;
- run under the per-(user, workspace) down-lane lock.

